Test Case: other_allow_extension_operations_disabled
================================================================================

Initial Error:
│ Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value
│
│   on azapi.tf line 48, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
│   48:       type         = identity.value.type
│     ├────────────────
│     │ identity.value is null
│
│ This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block is using can() to check if identity exists, but can() returns true even when the value is null. This causes the dynamic block to iterate with a null value, leading to the error when trying to access identity.value.type.
- Fix Method: Change the condition to check if the identity value is not null using != null instead of can()
- Changes Made: Modified azapi.tf line 46 from:
    for_each = can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
  to:
    for_each = module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
- Result: Success. Terraform plan now shows acceptable drift patterns only (resource-level attributes and Optional+Computed body fields).

Final Result: Fix successful

